arm64: dts: h713: hy300-pro - the lamp's PWM words stay, the PA12 pin group goes

test8 did not reach the login on the HY300 Pro (issue #1, 24.09.2026):
"sun50i-h713-pinctrl 2000000.pinctrl: unsupported function pwm5 on pin
PA12". 0166 put a pin group on the receiver node with the function name
"pwm5"; our pinctrl table knows no pwm5 anywhere, PA12's mux 2 is "pwm4"
there - so the receiver's default pinctrl could not be built, the receiver
never probed, /dev/video1 never appeared and h713-hdcp-key stayed in
"Starting".

The group was wrong on its facts as well: PA12 (vendor pwm4@0) is the AC200
codec's clock on both boards (ac200 tv_pwm_ch = 4, analysis A14), not the
lamp. The lamp's channel is the hardware PWM 5 of the board's
panel_config.ini [PWMSetting] (the HY310's ini names channel 2 = PB4, the
one that is not wired there); the vendor's pwm5@2000c15 node carries no
pins, so the pad is the firmware's business, as the panel registers are.

So the six words stay - they are the fix - and the pin group goes, along
with the pinctrl on the receiver node, so that no pin name can ever again
keep the receiver from probing. Which pad channel 5 drives is read from the
pin registers once the firmware runs with the words; it is not guessed here.

Follow-up to 0166, which stays byte-identical.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
@@ -47,32 +47,26 @@
 };
 
 /*
- * The lamp's dimmer. On this board it is a PWM the display firmware owns
- * and drives on PA12: the stock device tree muxes PA12 to its PWM function
- * with a pull-up (its pwm4@0 group, drive 10), and the board's
- * panel_config.ini [PWMSetting] says channel 5, polarity 1 (low active),
- * 40 kHz, vsync lock 1, duty 1..100, default_backlight 100 (both from the
- * owner's own dump, umbau/work/A12 and A14 material). The vendor's
- * PanelControl hands those six numbers to the firmware at start
- * (Thal_Vp_SetBacklightPwmInfo, AP3 3.5); the hdmirx driver does the same
- * with allwinner,backlight-pwm-info before it sends the level. Without
- * them the firmware never drives the dimmer and the picture is dark
- * (23.09.2026, the owner's photos against stock at the same exposure).
- * The pad's function is "pwm5" in the pinctrl table (mux 2, what the
- * vendor names pwm4); the value is what matters. The HY310's dimmer on
- * PB4 is not wired (cstenger 06.08.2026, A14), so it carries nothing here.
+ * The lamp's dimmer is a PWM the display firmware owns. The board's
+ * panel_config.ini [PWMSetting] says hardware channel 5, polarity 1 (low
+ * active), 40 kHz, vsync lock 1, duty 1..100 (the owner's own dump,
+ * umbau/work/A12 material), and the vendor's PanelControl hands those six
+ * numbers to the firmware at start (Thal_Vp_SetBacklightPwmInfo, AP3d
+ * 3.5) before it sends the level. The hdmirx driver does the same with
+ * allwinner,backlight-pwm-info. Without them the firmware never drives the
+ * dimmer and the picture is dark (23.09.2026, the owner's photos against
+ * stock at the same exposure). The HY310's ini names channel 2, PB4, which
+ * is not wired on that board (cstenger 06.08.2026, A14) - which is why the
+ * HY310 was never dark and carries nothing here.
+ *
+ * No pin group for it: the vendor's pwm5@2000c15 node names no pins, and
+ * PA12 (vendor pwm4, our pinctrl table's pwm4 on mux 2) is the AC200
+ * codec's clock on both boards (ac200 tv_pwm_ch = 4, A14), not the lamp.
+ * A pinctrl group on the receiver node with a function the table does not
+ * know ("pwm5") failed the receiver's probe and left test8 without a login
+ * (issue #1, 24.09.2026). Which pad channel 5 leaves the SoC on is to be
+ * read from the pin registers once the firmware runs with these words.
  */
-&pio {
-	bl_pwm_pa12_pin: bl-pwm-pa12-pin {
-		pins = "PA12";
-		function = "pwm5";
-		drive-strength = <10>;
-		bias-pull-up;
-	};
-};
-
 &hdmirx {
-	pinctrl-names = "default";
-	pinctrl-0 = <&bl_pwm_pa12_pin>;
 	allwinner,backlight-pwm-info = <5 1 40000 1 1 100>;
 };
